  "abi_findings": [
    "Purpose::ExecuteCommand=0 and LookForCommand=1 in the pinned source. The inspected caller and callee return the small WalkHandlersResult in x0; meaningful is byte 0, reserved byte 1, disabled byte 2, with a disengaged relevant-command Maybe when the word is 1.",
    "The pinned WidgetEvent flags are at offset 48: trusted bit 0, default-prevented bit 9, APZ-handled bit 23. Existing audited key/model conversion and actual process-role function are reused.",
    "Lookup returns a meaningful non-reserved native match. Gecko system capture calls its real remote-reply wait; its ordinary execution entry rejects prevented/untrusted events. Only accepted native execution invokes Gecko Event::PreventDefault.",
    "NSMenu performKeyEquivalent recursively matches actual native key equivalents and validates disabled state. The existing NSMenuView subclass only suppresses the matched actuation/highlighting step during key queries; no matching/drawing/geometry is copied."
  ],
  "separation": {
    "ui": "Append-only native query API uses the installed GNUstep menu implementation.",
    "bridge": "Existing key envelope/serialization and authenticated live owner/role route; no model registration or shortcut table is added.",
    "browser": "Only the small pinned adapter is compiled. Firefox/libxul/archive and installed AppKit remain unchanged.",
    "compiler": "Require Clang on AArch64; the compile guard is verified, with identical tested/current adapter bytes."
  },
